  <trk>
    <name>🇰🇷 Hallasan mountain - Seongpanak to Gwaneumsa - Wikiloc</name>
    <cmt>I climbed the Seongpanak trail and descended the Gwaneumsa trail. You can get to the start from the city by bus with one transfer. 
The trail is well-maintained along its entire length. There will either be a wooden walkway or stones, sometimes volcanic ones, to create an impression of the location (after all, we're climbing a volcano). 
 
You need to register your ascent before the hike: https://visithalla.jeju.go.kr/main/main.do?language=en_US 
 
I recommend arriving at the start no later than 9 a.m., and if you don't want to stand at the summit for an hour and a half to take a photo by the stone for your certificate, you should arrive even earlier. 
 
It took me about 2:50 to climb and about 2:30 to descend. Be sure to bring some sunscreen, a hat, water, and some food.</cmt>
    <desc>I climbed the Seongpanak trail and descended the Gwaneumsa trail. You can get to the start from the city by bus with one transfer. 
The trail is well-maintained along its entire length. There will either be a wooden walkway or stones, sometimes volcanic ones, to create an impression of the location (after all, we're climbing a volcano). 
 
You need to register your ascent before the hike: https://visithalla.jeju.go.kr/main/main.do?language=en_US 
 
I recommend arriving at the start no later than 9 a.m., and if you don't want to stand at the summit for an hour and a half to take a photo by the stone for your certificate, you should arrive even earlier. 
 
It took me about 2:50 to climb and about 2:30 to descend. Be sure to bring some sunscreen, a hat, water, and some food.</desc>
